WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.860
Hello I’m eerily Andrew Creepton

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.140
and you’re fiendishly watching Ghostly Weekly

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.700
Halloween is nigh,

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.680
and that means carving faces into produce,
stuffing pets into costumes,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.000
and playing Russian Roulette with Type-II
diabetes

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.750
by ingesting industrial-strength amounts of
candy.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.619
Perhaps you leave out bowls of sweets for
neighborhood trick-or-treaters.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.540
I don’t, because I believe in practical
gifts.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.060
And a bottle of ibuprofen for you!

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.440
Ever wonder what goes into the sugar that
goes into your coffee?

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.580
That sugar you’re buying costs more because
of sugar cronyism.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.020
And a bunch of sugar barons are getting rich
off of us suckers.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.240
Why?

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.000
Big Sugar.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.060
That’s not just my drag queen name,

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.240
it’s a reference to the special interests
who get rich off government protection.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.220
The sugar industry is a big cartel that meters
out fun white powder.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.860
It's like cocaine only it makes you fat, and
it’s legal and much less fun at parties.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.840
It’s indicative of a broader issue in our
country of crony capitalism.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.880
These tiny little green dots are where we
grow sugar cane.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.360
That’s because America’s climate is wonderfully,
spectacularly suited

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.060
to not grow sugar cane.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.640
Sugar magnates compensate for their crummy
business model

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.720
through subsidized loans and laws that protect
them from competition,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.960
inflating the price of sugar and ensuring
a sweet profit…

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.460
I SAID NO PUNS.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.620
We run our sugar industry with Soviet-style
central planning,

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.540
which, granted, has historically been a great
way to mass produce low-quality automobiles

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:30.920
and starvation.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.920
Let’s say there’s a surplus of sugar,

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.980
the government, has to buy the extra sugar
and resell it -- at a loss.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.760
Or if the market price drops below a certain
level,

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.260
the USDA has to activate sugar-for-ethanol
program to find the sugar industry new buyers.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.620
Not many other industries get that kind of
treatment.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.020
If nobody wants to buy my jokes I don’t
get to sell them to ethanol plants --

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.100
I have to give them for free to Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.320
[Rimshot]

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.160
When you add in the onerous tariffs the government
imposes on foreign sugar,

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.700
we're stuck with expensive American sugar,

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.300
which is also one of my drag names.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.780
Sugar costs are why Chicago is no longer the
candy capital of the world,

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:09.700
why Oreo and York Peppermint Patty and Hershey's
have moved out of the country,

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.120
and why Willy Wonka is dead.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.020
A report from the International Trade Administration

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.840
found that nearly three jobs in candy making
were lost

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.480
for every one sugar-growing job protected.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.340
Unnecessary handouts are indicative of a broader
issue in our economy.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.540
Sugar companies have a virtual monopoly on
production

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.180
but they don’t have a monopoly on handouts.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.080
Here’s a list of other industries that receive
unnecessary handouts.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.120
Slop around a few billion dollars here, and
a few billion dollars there,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.300
and pretty soon we’re robbing Americans
and jacking up the National Debt.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.080
Democrats and Republicans and libertarians
and Libertarians and Methodists

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.600
and my friend Steve,

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.680
should all come together to stop this sugary
graft.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.180
America’s sugar program is an unwieldy mechanism

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.420
designed to enrich a few plutocratic Sugar
Babies.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.240
I said no puns, I'm not gonna do one!

